-- 24: The world camera in closed form (Ghidra read-set, 2026-09-02).
-- Source doc: mvc-live-skins-quarters/docs/WORLD-CAMERA-GHIDRA.md. Apply with tools/re_kb/apply_seed.py (per statement).
-- Idempotent: UPSERT/UPDATE for nodes and existing edges; RELATE with explicit edge ids for new edges.
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:doc_world_camera_ghidra SET kind='doc', strength='code', ref='mvc-live-skins-quarters/docs/WORLD-CAMERA-GHIDRA.md', note='Ghidra read-set of the Steam world camera (2026-09-02): NaomiLib matrix stack, perspective and look-at closed forms, queue entry -> D3D (P,V)+W, camera-block writers, capture gate (1436 frames) reproducing camera_block.json.';

-- steam_routine roles (decompiled and read)
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140846a40 SET role='NaomiLib matrix stack init', note='ctx+0x1f80a4 mode, +0x1f80a8 prev mode, slots mode0 ctx+0x1f80ac / 1 +0x1f80ec / 2 +0x1f812c / 3 +0x1f816c (16 f32 row-major, row-vector convention), scratch +0x1f81c0 and +0x1f8200, push storage +0x1f81b0 depth +0x1f81b8/bc, proj offsets +0x1f8240/44 = 0, DAT_142ef0ab8 = &slot0. Identity source DAT_140ab20c0.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140846e90 SET role='matrix mode select (SH4 loc_8C1204F0)', note='if m<4: prev=mode; mode=m; DAT_142ef0ab8 = ctx+0x1f80ac + m*0x40. CONFIRMED pair by identical position/args in both camera routines.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140847ca0 SET role='matrix identity (SH4 loc_8C121100)', note='*cur = identity (copy of DAT_140ab20c0). CONFIRMED.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140846ee0 SET role='matrix pre-multiply', note='*cur = M x *cur (out[i][j] = sum_k M[i][k]*cur[k][j]). Used by perspective and look-at.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_1408473d0 SET role='matrix post-multiply', note='*cur = *cur x M. Used to compose V x P x Screen for point projection / sort keys.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140846880 SET role='transform point by current matrix', note='out = [x y z 1] x *cur (row vector).';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140848200 SET role='projection x/y offset (SH4 loc_8C121710)', note='ctx+0x1f8240 = ox, +0x1f8244 = oy. Camera passes (0, blk+0x6988 = -0.41). SH4 stores fabs() to 0x8C16BD80/84 and 8C1219B0 consumes+zeroes them. CONFIRMED pair.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140847f20 SET role='perspective matrix (SH4 loc_8C1219B0)', note='P(angle u16, aspect, near, far): t=tan(angle*2pi/65536*0.5); h=atan(t*240/320); cot=cos(h)/sin(h); P=[cot/aspect 0 0 0; 0 cot 0 0; -ox -oy -(f+n)/(f-n) -1; 0 0 -2fn/(f-n) 0]; *cur = P x *cur; ctx+0x1f8518=0. Constants read from dump: DAT_1408e2a68=6.2831855, DAT_14092a584=1/65536, DAT_1408e2a44=0.5, DAT_14097da6c=240, DAT_14097d594=320, DAT_1408e34a4=-1.0. fov 43 -> P00=2.53862, P11=3.38482 (matches camera_block.json rows 15-18 to 4.7e-7). CONFIRMED.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140846c80 SET role='look-at matrix (SH4 loc_8C11FF90)', note='L(eye,target,roll u16): d=normalize(eye-target); r=normalize(cross((0,1,0),d)); u=cross(d,r); L rows [r.x u.x d.x 0][r.y u.y d.y 0][r.z u.z d.z 0][-eye.r -eye.u -eye.d 1]; if roll: *cur = Rz(roll) x *cur (sin table DAT_142ef0ac0 / cos DAT_142f30ac0); *cur = L x *cur. Fight camera (target=(eye.x,eye.y,0), roll 0) gives V = translate(-eye) == camera_block.json rows 7-10. CONFIRMED.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_14061d7e0 SET role='world camera setup x1 (deck, lists 5/6)', note='slot3 = P(angle=(blk+0x6974*65536/360+0.5)&0xFFFF [constant _DAT_1408fefd0 = 65536.0, NOT 32768], aspect DAT_14095e268=1.3333334, near ctx+0x1f82b0 (=1.0, written by FUN_140620960 each frame), far DAT_140a6e518=1400000.0, offsets (0, blk+0x6988)); slot2 = LookAt(blk+0x6914.., blk+0x695C.., roll blk+0x698C); leaves mode 1 (world) current. CONFIRMED (== loc_8c02e1a4).';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_14061d6a0 SET role='world camera setup x0.1 (lists 7/8/9)', note='same as FUN_14061d7e0 with eye/target * DAT_1408e2f64 (0.1) and far _DAT_14097d5ec = 12000.0. camera_block.json list7 rows reproduce with these values (2.7e-4 abs).';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_14061d5b0 SET role='fixed 90-degree projection + identity view (HUD list 0xB, list 0xC parts)', note='slot3 = P(0x4000, 4/3, ctx+0x1f82b0=1.0, 12000) with offsets (0,0) -> rows [1,0,0,0][0,1.3333,0,0][0,0,-1.000167,-1][0,0,-2.000167,0]; slot2 = identity. This is the projection-only scene CB seen on 25 identity-CBWorld draws of frame 4445. CONFIRMED.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_1408436a0 SET role='NaomiLib queue append (kind, entry 0x130)', note='kinds 2..5: entry+8 = slot3 (P), +0x48 = slot2 (V), +0x88 = slot1 (W). kinds 0,1,6,7: +0x48 = IDENTITY, +0x88 = slot1. Sort key = FUN_140843320(record centre) through V x P x Screen. CONFIRMED.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140842e30 SET role='queue flush to D3D command ring', note='per entry: FUN_1400483c0(4, entry+8, 0x80) = P and V (128 B, the host builds the 432-B scene CB from these), FUN_1400483c0(7, entry+0x88, 0x40) = W (CBWorld); kinds 0-3 -> FUN_1408482a0, 4/5 -> FUN_140848ce0, 6/7 -> FUN_140849030. CONFIRMED.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_1408482a0 SET role='polygon consumer kinds 0-3 (raw vertices)', note='copies each vertex pos/normal/uv verbatim into a 0x28-B VB (FUN_140048370 stride 0x28); FUN_140846960 rotates the normal for lighting colour only. NO CPU position transform. The deck, list 5/6 nodes, HUD and list-0xC parts all take this path. CONFIRMED.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140848ee0 SET role='NaomiLib object record walk', note='walks records from obj+0x18 while (int)PCW<0 (next = rec + rec[0x13] + 0x50), optional arena copy, FUN_1408436a0(kind, &rec, 0x130). Submits RAW model vertices; the deck uses kind 2 with W = identity. CONFIRMED.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_14061c6e0 SET role='match camera init (SH4 loc_8c02e014)', note='eye=(0,95,320/tan(0x0F4A)=812.357 via FUN_140845170=tanf(u16)), target=(0,95,0), fov blk+0x6974=43.0, blk+0x6988=-0.41 (proj y-offset), state bytes 0x6908/0x690f/0x6910/0x6911/0x6912=0, bounds 0x69a0=-1280 0x69a4=1280 0x69a8=1238.4 0x69ac=-46.6, ctx+0x1f82b0=0.1. CONFIRMED pair: SH4 pool at 8c02e014 holds 0x0F4A, 0x422c0000, 0xbed1eb85, 0x42be0000, 0x43a00000.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_14061caf0 SET role='fight camera re-init (first fight frame)', note='identical body to FUN_14061c6e0 then blk+0x690f++. Called from FUN_14061ca70 case 0.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_14061ca70 SET role='per-frame camera state machine (blk+0x6908)', note='0 = fight camera (FUN_14061caf0 once, then FUN_14061ce90 every frame); 1 = scripted: 0x690f 0 -> load key 0 of script blk+0x6910 from PTR_DAT_140a6e460/488, 1 -> FUN_14061c0a0, 2 -> hold; 2..5 = round transitions. Also snapshots 0x6914..->0x6920.. and 0x695C..->0x6968.. CONFIRMED.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_14061ce90 SET role='fight camera update (every frame)', note='FIRST copies 0x6914..1C -> 0x6920..28 and 0x695C..64 -> 0x6968..70 (so 0x6920 = previous frame eye); 0x69bc = 812.357; x-follow FUN_14061a0c0 (P1) / FUN_14061a370 (P2) from fighter +0x50 clamped by FUN_14061c660 (0x69a0/0x69a4); y+zoom FUN_140619dd0 / FUN_14061a1a0 / FUN_14061a450; tail: 0x6990 = eye.x-320, 0x6994 = eye.x+320, 0x69b0 = eye.y+98.4, 0x6998/0x699c = 0x69b0 +/- 240. CONFIRMED.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140619dd0 SET role='fight camera y/zoom target (both fighters)', note='0x6980 = max_i(y_i(+0x54) + byte(+0x180)*2.142857 [0 if state +1 in 0x18..0x1A]) - 350 when >0; 0x69b8 = clamp(0x6980+95, 95, 900); eye.y = target.y smoothed 0.25 toward 0x69b8; eye.z toward 0x69bc (812.357); target.z toward 0x69c8 (0). Hence target == (eye.x, eye.y, 0) and zoom constant in the fight state. CONFIRMED.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_14061a0c0 SET role='fight camera x-follow (P1)', note='0x69b4 = fighter(0x6a08)+0x50 clamped; eye.x = target.x smoothed by 1/N toward it. CONFIRMED.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_14061c0a0 SET role='scripted camera keyframe interpolation', note='tables PTR_DAT_140a6e438 (count + frame counts) / 460 (eye,target 6 f32 per key) / 488 (orbit deg: eye-orbit xyz, target-orbit xy, roll); linear eye/target interpolation; FUN_14061ae80 orbits eye about target; FUN_14061b8e0 orbits target about eye and writes roll blk+0x698C = (deg*65536/360+0.5)&0xFFFF. Script 4 = eye (0,95,812.357) -> target (0,190,0) for 60 frames (tilted). CONFIRMED.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140844a10 SET role='renderer constants + sin/cos tables', note='DAT_140ab2080 = Screen matrix [320 0 0 0; 0 -240 0 0; 0 0 1 0; 320 240 0 1]; ctx+0x1f82b0 = 1.0; builds 65536-entry sin (DAT_142ef0ac0) / cos (DAT_142f30ac0) tables used by FUN_140845150/FUN_1408444d0. CONFIRMED.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140845170 SET role='tanf(u16 angle)', note='FUN_140817230(angle * 2pi/65536). 320/tan(0x0F4A) = 812.357 = the constant zoom.';

-- recompiles edges: promote to confirmed
UPDATE recompiles:FUN_140846e90_loc_8c1204f0 SET confidence='confirmed', method='seed+decompile', evidence='same call slot/args in loc_8c02e1a4 vs FUN_14061d7e0; SH4 saves XMTRX to slot, sets mode byte 0x8C2D68E4, reloads via 8C1201E0; Steam moves DAT_142ef0ab8 to ctx+0x1f80ac+m*0x40 (WORLD-CAMERA-GHIDRA.md s1)';
UPDATE recompiles:FUN_140847ca0_loc_8c121100 SET confidence='confirmed', method='seed+decompile', evidence='both write the identity (WORLD-CAMERA-GHIDRA.md s1)';
UPDATE recompiles:FUN_140848200_loc_8c121710 SET confidence='confirmed', method='seed+decompile', evidence='SH4 stores fabs(fr4),fabs(fr5) to 0x8C16BD80/84 (consumed by 8C1219B0); Steam stores to ctx+0x1f8240/44 (consumed by FUN_140847f20); same call slot (WORLD-CAMERA-GHIDRA.md s1)';
UPDATE recompiles:FUN_140847f20_loc_8c1219b0 SET confidence='confirmed', method='seed+decompile', evidence='same 4 args (angle u16, aspect, near, far) and call slot; Steam closed form read; SH4 body uses sin/atan/cos helpers 8C11EB20/8C11E170/8C11E2E0 and ftrv loader 8C120540 (not reduced) (WORLD-CAMERA-GHIDRA.md s1/2.1)';
UPDATE recompiles:FUN_140846c80_loc_8c11ff90 SET confidence='confirmed', method='seed+decompile', evidence='same args (eye, target, u16 roll) and call slot; SH4 computes target-eye, normalises, translates by -eye via 8C1210C0 (WORLD-CAMERA-GHIDRA.md s1/2.2)';
UPDATE recompiles:FUN_14061c6e0_loc_8c02e014 SET confidence='confirmed', method='seed+constants', evidence='unique constant set {0x0F4A, 0x422c0000 (43.0), 0xbed1eb85 (-0.41), 0x42be0000 (95), 0x43a00000 (320)} in the pool at 8c02e014..; Steam FUN_14061c6e0 writes the same to blk+0x6914..0x6988 (WORLD-CAMERA-GHIDRA.md s5)';

-- globals: corrections and additions
UPDATE global:camera_nearfar SET note='CORRECTED 2026-09-02: NOT near/far. 0x6988 (stage struct +0x80) = projection Y-OFFSET fed to FUN_140848200 (P[2][1] = -offset = +0.41 in the scene CB); 0x698C (+0x84) = u16 ROLL angle for the look-at (FUN_140846c80 param_3), written by the scripted camera FUN_14061b8e0, 0 in the fight state. near = ctx+0x1f82b0 = 1.0, far = 1400000 (x1) / 12000 (x0.1, HUD).', type='f32 + u16';
UPDATE global:camera_lookat SET note='camera look-at x/y/z; stage struct +0x54/58/5C. Fight state: == (eye.x, eye.y, 0) on all 1436 captured frames (FUN_140619dd0 keeps target.y = eye.y, target.z -> 0). Free in the scripted state (blk+0x6908 == 1): e.g. script 4 = target (0,190,0) with eye (0,95,812.357).';
UPDATE global:camera_eye SET note='render camera eye x / y / zoom; stage struct +0xC/+0x10/+0x14. zoom = 320/tan(0x0F4A) = 812.357 constant in the fight state (FUN_14061c6e0 sets it, FUN_140619dd0 smooths toward 0x69bc = the same constant). eye.x follows the fighters (FUN_14061a0c0), eye.y = clamp(max fighter y - 350, 0, 805) + 95 smoothed. Consumed by FUN_14061d7e0 (deck, lists 5/6) and x0.1 by FUN_14061d6a0.';
UPDATE global:camera_fov SET note='camera FOV in degrees (43.0 in a match, set by FUN_14061c6e0); horizontal: both builds compute angle = (fov*65536/360+0.5)&0xffff (constant 0x47800000 = 65536.0, not 32768) and the vertical half-angle = atan(tan(angle/2)*240/320); P00 = cot(vhalf)/1.3333 = 2.53862, P11 = cot(vhalf) = 3.38482.';
UPSERT global:camera_prev_eye SET addr='0x8C26A530', steam_off='0x6920', type='f32[3]', note='previous-frame snapshot of blk+0x6914..0x691C (copied at the top of FUN_14061ce90 before the update; 0x6968..0x6970 = same for the look-at). Read by FUN_140620f10 (only 0x6928 = zoom) and FUN_140620740 (billboard flag bits 7/8). Lags eye by exactly one frame on 988/1436 captured frames.';
UPSERT global:camera_state SET addr='0x8C26A518', steam_off='0x6908', type='u8[5]', note='camera state bytes: 0x6908 = mode (0 fight, 1 scripted, 2..5 round transitions), 0x690f = sub-state, 0x6910 = script index into PTR_DAT_140a6e438/460/488, 0x6911 = key index, 0x6912. FUN_14061ca70. A tape needs the 9 camera floats + roll only when 0x6908 != 0.';
UPSERT global:camera_window SET addr='0x8C26A5A0', steam_off='0x6990', type='f32[6]', note='sprite-system screen window derived each frame from the CURRENT eye (FUN_14061ce90 tail): 0x6990 = eye.x-320, 0x6994 = eye.x+320, 0x6998 = 0x69b0+240, 0x699c = 0x69b0-240, 0x69b0 = eye.y+98.4.';
UPSERT global:nl_matrix_slots SET addr='ctx+0x1f80ac', steam_off='ctx+0x1f80ac', type='f32[4][16]', note='Steam-only NaomiLib matrix slots: mode0 ctx+0x1f80ac, mode1 (WORLD) +0x1f80ec, mode2 (VIEW) +0x1f812c, mode3 (PROJ) +0x1f816c; current pointer DAT_142ef0ab8. Queue entries copy P (+8), V (+0x48), W (+0x88); D3D gets (P,V) as command 4 (128 B) and W as command 7 (64 B).';
UPSERT global:nl_near_plane SET addr='ctx+0x1f82b0', steam_off='ctx+0x1f82b0', type='f32', note='near plane for all three projection setups; FUN_140620960 writes 1.0 at the top of every render frame (FUN_14061c6e0 writes 0.1 earlier, overwritten). far = DAT_140a6e518 = 1400000 (FUN_14061d7e0) or 12000 (FUN_14061d6a0, FUN_14061d5b0).';

-- findings
UPSERT finding:world_camera_closed_form SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-02', contribution_candidate=true, note='The deck/list 5-6 camera is V = LookAt(blk+0x6914.., blk+0x695C.., roll blk+0x698C) and P = Persp(angle=(blk+0x6974*65536/360+0.5)&0xFFFF, aspect 4/3, near 1.0, far 1400000, y-offset blk+0x6988); the D3D 432-B scene CB = [V.P | eye,2f/(f+n) | forward,100 | (c,1/c) | V | V^-1 | P | P^-1 | (V.P)^-1] with c = 20.41504 (far 1.4e6) / 13.55109 (far 12000). Reproduces camera_block.json on the 1436 captured frames: max abs err 0.0121 (rows 25/26, values ~400, rel 3e-5); rows 0-3/15-18 to float32 rounding. x0.1 variant: 2.7e-4. Rows 4-6 are INFERRED (host builder for D3D command 4 not located).';
UPSERT finding:fight_camera_lookat_equals_eye_xy SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-02', contribution_candidate=true, note='In camera state 0 (blk+0x6908 == 0) the look-at is (eye.x, eye.y, 0), zoom = 812.357, fov = 43, offset = -0.41, roll = 0: 0 violations over 1436 captured frames (capgate/state), and by construction of FUN_140619dd0/FUN_14061a0c0. A tape carrying stage_id + blk+0x6914/18/1C is sufficient in this state.';
UPSERT finding:camera_not_per_stage SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-02', contribution_candidate=true, note='No per-stage initialiser (PTR_PTR_140a6ec20[stage]) writes any camera field. The complete writer set of blk+0x6914..0x691C/0x695C..0x6964/0x6974/0x6988/0x698C (fingerprint scan of all functions, then decompiled) is FUN_14061c6e0, FUN_14061caf0, FUN_14061ca70, FUN_14061ce90, FUN_14061a0c0/a370, FUN_140619dd0/a1a0/a450, FUN_14061c0a0/ae80/b8e0, FUN_140615020, FUN_1406285f0, FUN_140629890, FUN_14062bc80, FUN_140607da0 (debug). Stage id enters nowhere. The stage-15/2 deck garble is therefore not a per-stage camera constant.';
UPSERT finding:scripted_camera_state_1 SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-02', contribution_candidate=true, note='blk+0x6908 == 1 runs keyframe scripts (PTR_DAT_140a6e438/460/488, index blk+0x6910): eye and look-at interpolate independently, FUN_14061ae80/FUN_14061b8e0 orbit them and write roll blk+0x698C. Script 4 = eye (0,95,812.357) -> target (0,190,0) x60 frames = a tilted camera. Under a script the tape must carry the 9 floats + u16 roll (or the state bytes 0x6908/0x690f/0x6910/0x6911 and the frame counter).';
UPSERT finding:sprite_walker_camera_is_prev_frame SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-02', note='blk+0x6920/24/28 (and 0x6968..) = previous frame eye/look-at: copied at the top of FUN_14061ce90 before the update; measured 1-frame lag on 988/1436 frames. The sprite walker reads only 0x6928 (zoom) and places sprites via the window fields 0x6990.. derived from the CURRENT 0x6914/0x6918; so tape eyeX/eyeY/zoom = 0x6914/0x6918/0x691C is right for sprites and deck alike; 0x6920 matters only for billboard nodes (FUN_140620740 bits 7/8).';
UPSERT finding:deck_and_lists_raw_vertices_kind2 SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-02', contribution_candidate=true, note='FUN_140848ee0 -> FUN_1408436a0(kind 2) -> FUN_140842e30 -> FUN_1408482a0: model vertices are copied verbatim (no CPU transform); the D3D layer receives (P,V) via command 4 and W via command 7. Deck: W = identity; list 5/6 nodes: W = node+0xA8. The projection-only scene CB [1,0,0,0][0,1.3333,0,0][0,0,-1.000167,-1][0,0,-2.000167,0] is FUN_14061d5b0 (angle 0x4000, far 12000, V = I) used by the HUD (FUN_140620ea0) and list-0xC parts (FUN_140653a70); their small z=-71 vertices are authored in view space, not CPU-transformed.';
UPSERT finding:training_deck_absent_from_capture_open SET status='open', confidence='medium', date='2026-09-02', note='FUN_140620960 submits *(u64*)PTR_DAT_142edf588 (stage model 0, kind 2, W = I) on every mode-0 frame with stage != 8, yet frame 4445 (stage 0x0B) has only 6 identity-CBWorld draws (giant quads x +/-6244, z -65000..500) matching NO model of the STG0B rip (no rip model exceeds +/-5000), while the rip model 0 is 2 meshes / 2424 verts (x +/-2500, y -182..1363, z -2895..816). Either live table entry 0 != rip model 0 (ordering) or its records are empty/culled. Test: live read *(u64*)0x142edf630, walk records (next = rec + rec[0x13] + 0x50 while PCW<0), count vertices vs 2424. Same question as the stage-15 garble.';
UPSERT finding:stage15_deck_garble_owner_open SET status='open', confidence='medium', date='2026-09-02', note='Bisection before any renderer edit: (1) on a garbled stage-15/2 frame read blk+0x6908/0x690f/0x6910 and the 9 camera floats + roll; if state 0 and target == (eye.x,eye.y,0) the camera is ruled out (the closed form is general); if 0x6908 == 1 carry the floats. (2) draw a list-5 node and model 0 with the same identity W + closed-form CB; list-5 exact and model 0 wrong => model-0 geometry path (rip model order / record walk / scale) owns it. (3) live vertex-count check of table entry 0 vs the rip.';
UPSERT finding:fov_constant_is_65536 SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-02', note='The angle conversion in FUN_14061d7e0/FUN_14061d6a0 and loc_8c02e1a4/8c02e246 is fov*65536/360 (+0.5, &0xFFFF): _DAT_1408fefd0 = 0x47800000 = 65536.0f read from the dump; the SH4 pool word 0x47800000 at loc_8c02e31c is the same value. The earlier note saying 32768 was a decimal slip; 43 deg -> 7828 -> half-angle 21.5 deg.';

